386	\caption{Variance decomposition of hotspot detection performance. Among modeled factors, the scoring $\times$ pathogen interaction ($\omega^2 = 0.296$) is the largest component, exceeding all main effects and other two-way interactions. A within-cell residual $\omega^2 \approx 0.39$---accounting for the unmodeled three-way interaction and parameter-variant noise---is shown for reference.}
